  "result": "Perfect! All 106 tests pass \u2713. I've successfully added VAT calculation to the invoicing system:\n\n**src/invoices.js:**\n- Added `lineVat(line)` function that calculates VAT per line on the amount **after discount**, using `roundCents()` for precision\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }` where:\n  - `vat` is the sum of all line VATs (rounded per line, not a percentage of total)\n  - `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n  - All amounts clamped to >= 0 (never negative)\n\n**src/render.js:**\n- Updated to import `lineVat` function\n- Shows VAT on its own line (`VAT: \u20acX.XX`) just above the total line\n- Only shows VAT line if `vat > 0`\n- Maintains proper formatting for all price displays\n\n**Tests (106/106 passing):**\n- 14 new VAT-specific tests in invoices.test.js covering:\n  - Line VAT calculation on amounts after discount\n  - VAT with 0% rates\n  - Mixed VAT rates\n  - Total calculations with VAT and discounts\n  - Example calculations (services with tier discounts)\n- 4 new VAT rendering tests in render.test.js covering:\n  - VAT line display\n  - Multiple items with VAT\n  - Suppressing VAT line when not present\n  - Combined discount and VAT rendering\n- Updated ~20 existing tests to account for VAT in totals\n\nThe implementation correctly handles:\n- Per-line rounding with `roundCents()`\n- Discount applied before VAT calculation\n- Tier discounts combined with line discounts\n- No negative amounts (clamped to 0)",
